 "verdict": "REJECTED as a gfx1100 dense bulk-prefill replacement: the retained float Q4T16 WMMA owners win 9/9 case-rows. Best integer-MMQ totals (DS4 pack + consumes) reach only 0.205-0.216x the per-matrix T16 owner time on the ffn gate/up pair, 0.402-0.542x on ffn_down and 0.387-0.481x on attention_q; ratios are flat or worsening with rows (512/1024/4096). The efa4e8641-family load-reuse deltas are within +-3% (not load-bound), matching the C8 campaign's raw-MMQ32 MLP-limited finding. Pack cost is negligible (0.029-0.816 ms); the consumer kernels are the blocker, consistent with the 2026-08-12 T16-payload integer rejections and the 2026-06-16 selected-shape raw ds4 measurements. This closes the last nasone32 projection donor hypothesis for the PP8192 gap: combined with the 2026-09-09 VDR decode screen, the fork's raw-Q4_K x Q8_1 arithmetic class loses to the T16 float owners on both decode GEMV and bulk prefill on this stack. The kernels, bit-exact ctl/vdr harness and DS4 CPU oracle are retained as leaf evidence for future integer prefill routes.",
